A||||9||BroCar 87||Rear end is swaying at 60 mph WHY????||||11||
Z||000000||BroCar 87||09-30-2000||07:56 PM||||As the topic states, my back end is swaying around when I hit around 57. BUT once I get up to 70 mph it stops swaying. SOOOOO the drive is good up to about 57 then up to 70 it feels like **** ... swaying back and forth from left to right and left to right, but when I get up to 70 mph and more, it stops the swaying. WHY???????<BR>I DID just put new tires on the back. both are the 215's. WOULD THAT BE PART OF PROBLEM? <BR>I love the 215's on the back too. They feel soo much better when I make a turn. MORE control. I have 195's on front.<BR>Any help is greatly appreciated!! thanks<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NorthFLFieroSIG.jpg">    <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||11
Z||000001||theogre||09-30-2000||08:01 PM||||crappy old cradle bushings or A arm bushings could do it. The tires could do it themselves or just agravate the hell out of  a cradle problem.<P>Before I put the polly cradle set in mine the cross winds would move the whole rear of the car when going down the highway.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BroCar 87||09-30-2000||08:05 PM||||YEA!!! Sounds like a good answer to me. But would that do it only at that particular speed? Ohhh wait. ALSO, my motor mounts are shot, The only good one is the dogbone. Could that also be a factor?? WOW, I would have never thought of this on my own... THANKS theogre<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NorthFLFieroSIG.jpg">    <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fearless Freep||09-30-2000||08:08 PM||||Yah know...my car had been handling like crap for the past couple weeks.  The front end had been sqeeking like a mattress.  Figured that I was going to have to bite the bullet and do some bushings....Well.....<P>Pulled into the gas station and discovered that I had about 15psi in the front tires and about 20 in the rear!!  Low and behold....filled em up to about 32 and things are a rocking! Even the squeek as gone.  Whats my point????  Check the easy things first, you may save yourself a few bucks.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BroCar 87||09-30-2000||09:18 PM||||Thanks Fearless. The tires I have on there now, are off my other fiero. They are different brands and different "max psi" settings. One is 44 the other 35. What would be a good tire pressure for them to equal out at?<BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NorthFLFieroSIG.jpg">    <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||14
Z||000005||Fearless Freep||09-30-2000||09:23 PM||||I usually leave all mine at around 32psi.  Course (I will have to go look at the model of my tires) but I find that 32 usually gives me a good even wear.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fearless Freep||09-30-2000||09:42 PM||||Hmmmm so I suppose to balance them out.......damn it I always hated those friggin (if train A is moving at 65mph and train B is moving at 40mph) questions......I would figure that if you run the 35's at about 32psi then the 44's should be around 40psi??  Somebody wanna check behind me here???||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||09-30-2000||10:58 PM||||mis mactched tires could easily cause this. inflation pressure is a factor to.<P>the reason for this happening in a particular speed range is likely some very low frequency harmonics. In that speed range you hit a "sweet spot" and the car starts singing.<P>Motor mounts could add to or cause this. The mounts load the cradle. The strut loads the body. If the motor can shift around easy it can push/pull on the right side of the cradle bad.  The right side will move more than the left because of the strut being so far that way.<P>There are likely a combination of things adding up in some bizar way to cause this. I'd start with replacment of the cradle bushings and motor mounts.||||reg||1
Z||000008||DjKid||10-01-2000||01:05 AM||||So A Dead Motor Mount could cause this? I'm hoping thats my problem, cuz i'm currently strapped for money, unemployed..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Anyone feel like donating to the 'Help Ray fix his Fiero Fund'?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hehe.. j/k ya'll.. but any help you could give me in advice would be more than welcome. All help is always appreciated to the fullest. Ya'll group of guys & gals.. are the best. I'd not have a Fiero if it weren't for ya'll.<P>------------------<BR>Ray - Blue 88 Coupe - <A HREF="http://blueknight.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>My Blue Knight</A> - <A HREF="http://www.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank> Carolina Fieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||BroCar 87||10-01-2000||05:51 PM||||Well I finally just sat in my car and thought  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> . My car didn't sway before I put these other tires on the back. Maybe one of the tires is messed up or warped or something. I pull off the passenger side rear tire and there it is. A bubble in the inside side wall of the tire. I put on a p195 instead of the 215 and test drove it. PERFECT RIDE AGAIN. <BR>Now that brings up another question. Can I run p215 on the driver side and p195 on the passenger's? What are the consequenses? I know I am going to have to get them the same size, but what kind of harm am I doing until they do get swapped?<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NorthFLFieroSIG.jpg">    <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||1
